  "about": "The introitus of the formulary “Saint Joseph the Worker” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Wisdom rendered to the just the reward of their labors, and led them by a wonderful way: and she was to them a shelter by day, and a light of stars by night. Alleluia, alleluia. Unless the Lord builds the house, those who build it labor in vain. Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen. Wisdom rendered to the just the reward of their labors, and led them by a wonderful way: and she was to them a shelter by day, and a light of stars by night. Alleluia, alleluia.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w005", "w006"], "anchor": "w005", "gloss": "of their labors" }, { "words": ["w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w042", "gloss": "to the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w053", "w054", "w055"], "anchor": "w054", "gloss": "forever and ever" }, { "words": ["w061", "w062"], "anchor": "w061", "gloss": "of their labors" }] }
  },
